<speak>
i am allowed to put myself first.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to make mistakes and still be worthy.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to say no without explaining.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to take up space without guilt.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to disappoint people and still be good.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to want more than survival.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to let others carry their own feelings.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to be loved simply for who i am.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to change my mind.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to outgrow people and places.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to feel joy even when others don’t.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to rest without earning it.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to speak my truth, even if my voice shakes.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to set boundaries and keep them.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to choose peace over proving myself.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to heal at my own pace.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to take up dreams bigger than my fear.
<break time="600ms"/>
i am allowed to be whole, even if i was once broken.
<break time="600ms"/>
try to go 48 hours without apologizing unless you truly caused harm.
<break time="600ms"/>
what emotions came up when you stopped apologizing?
<break time="600ms"/>
anxiety? freedom?
<break time="600ms"/>
